From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:50:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Follow touches as well as pointer motion

The eyes are redrawn on raw motion events.  A touch screen driven by
libinput is a touch device: its contacts move the pointer through pointer
emulation, but its raw events are RawTouchBegin, RawTouchUpdate and
RawTouchEnd, never RawMotion, so the eyes stayed still while the cursor
followed every touch.  Select the raw touch events too; each one redraws
from the pointer's position as raw motion does.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted
---
 Eyes.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Eyes.c b/Eyes.c
--- a/Eyes.c
+++ b/Eyes.c
@@ -343,8 +343,12 @@
 
     memset(mask1, 0, sizeof(mask1));
 
-    /* select for button and key events from all master devices */
+    /* select for raw motion from all master devices, and for raw touches:
+       a touch screen moves the pointer, but its raw events are touches */
     XISetMask(mask1, XI_RawMotion);
+    XISetMask(mask1, XI_RawTouchBegin);
+    XISetMask(mask1, XI_RawTouchUpdate);
+    XISetMask(mask1, XI_RawTouchEnd);
 
     evmasks[0].deviceid = XIAllMasterDevices;
     evmasks[0].mask_len = sizeof(mask1);
